{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals","id":1220884,"title":"Need Advice on Creating Elementals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-21T11:33:14-07:00","id":1220884,"title":"Need Advice on Creating Elementals","content":"I\u2019ve been trying to build some elementals and it\u2019s just not working. Does anyone have any advice about how they come up with cool interesting elementals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:49:04-07:00","id":1220891,"title":"","content":"When I was doing elementals for Thousand Sanctioned Beasts, I generally started by figuring out some way in which they restore or alter the balance of the elements (although this is not actually why they exist in the current edition). Muchmosses garden, weatheralls shape coastlines, and achenes express the bounty of the earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T12:16:32-07:00","id":1220899,"title":"","content":"What kind of elements are they to represent?<br /> <br /> IMO elementals - especially low level ones - are just marginally more sentient than a magical golem. They are living forces of nature after all... its first if they reach maybe essence 3 that they would reach full sentience.<br /> <br /> While essence 2, it would be on par with a wild animal - but with a twist: it would be an 'animal' expression of the element they're embodying.<br /> <br /> So... water elementals of a raging river with strong currents? strong but mindless wall bulls that seem impossible to physically stop. summoning a couple of these and chaining them to a ship with sturdy black jade-steel chains can allow for a ship to be pulled along as if flowing downstream in a river, anywhere in the water.<br /> <br /> wood elementals that effect plant-growth in a forest? Their level of activity would depend on how much wood essence is in the area for them to work with - they could seem very dormant if operating in a shrub desert, where plants grow slowly - or be manic buzzing bees in the east, making things grow all the time. In the realm these are constantly summoned to improve farm yields.<br /> <br /> their bodies would be informed by their purpose and their element - of course - so an earth elemental that consumes fallen leaves and whatnot to produce dirt would be a wolf-sized earth-worm that just mindlessly and constantly gobbles up organic matter and poops out highly fertile dirt. (never mind that a lot of sorcerers summon these things to do away with corpses quickly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T07:52:14-07:00","id":1221154,"title":"","content":"Cloud People are Essence 2 and they seem fully sentient, quite smart in fact. In the Core, Tidemares (Essence 2) are capable of speech but they're not too bright and tend towards inane gossip. Meanwhile, young Greenmaws (Essence 3) are much more feral. I think elementals are probably <i>less likely</i> to be of animal-level intelligence the higher their Essence rating, but it isn't absolute. <br /> <br /> As for how to come up with cool elementals, a few suggested methods...<br /> <br /> 1) If you're better at coming up with interesting characters than magical species, try to create an interesting character who is an elemental, and reverse engineer their species from there, taking into consideration how they embody or differ from each aspect of their species archetype so that you don't create an entire race of &quot;this guy&quot;. <br /> <br /> For my young Zenith sorcerer, I came up with an earth elemental companion called Aiax (that's his given name, not his species name). He's a small pangolin made of rough stone, and can burrow through earth as fast as a fish can swim. He can roll into a ball and become much more durable, but can't attack and can only move by rolling clumsily. He <i>used</i> to have a humanoid form that looked like a stone warrior in pangolin-scale armour, and was quite the swordmaster, but he recently lost the ability to take that form for some reason and doesn't want to talk about it. He's generally a creature of few words, but wise. Also lazy. And keeps demanding shoes even though his feet are made of rock. How am I going to explain to a cobbler that I need two sets of sturdy boots for baby-sized feet, Aiax? <br /> <br /> 2) Straight-up steal. Trawl folk tales for creatures that could be adapted into elementals. Trawl video games like Monster Hunter, Final Fantasy or Pokemon. Trawl popular culture in general. Import them into Creation and knead their concept a bit until it blends with the setting. Do some palette swaps or rename the creature if you want. <br /> <br /> Cambodia has legends about a deer that breathes underwater through gills on its muzzle. Filipino/Spanish myth has Ibong Adarna, a magical bird whose songs can heal and whose poop can turn a man to stone. China has the Shangyang or rainbird, whose dances herald heavy rains. There's also a Chinese tree-spirit called a Penghou, which looks like a black dog with no tail (and possibly a human face) which apparently tastes like dog meat when cooked (seriously, every source mentions that you should eat this thing). Hey, how about centaurs, right, but with their back-legs replaced with fish-tails! Too silly for Exalted? Not too silly for Greek mythology! Meet Ichthyocentaurs! South Africa gives us Grootslang, a massive elephant-serpent with keen intellect and cunning, a taste for cruelty, and a lust for gems. The basilisk turns creatures to stone, pick your favourite interpretation of its appearance. Have we mentioned naga yet? <br /> <br /> I'm not even going to start on Pokemon. Find an online pokedex and browse. If the pictures don't spark ideas, the pokedex entries will. Search the wiki of your favourite monster-fighting game if you're not into Pokemon. <br /> <br /> 3) Take an animal. Add an element. Now add a twist or cool feature not directly related to the element, something you could use as a story hook maybe.<br /> <br /> Fire-horse ... crap that's a Pokemon. Oh well, let's forge on and make it our own. Let's see, a hook. If you stare ahead into its fiery mane while riding a wild fire-horse at breakneck speed, you will see true visions about past and future events in your life. Surviving this ordeal is the only way to begin taming the beast, after which its fire will no longer burn you, but will also no longer grant you visions. Needs a name. Pyremane? Sounds cool but has deathy connotations not otherwise present in the creature's themes ... although it will absolutely burn you to death if you can't resist damage from magical fire, so maybe it's not too inappropriate. Kludging together some Persian names gives Azaroya (fire+dream/vision). That'll do. <br /> <br /> 4) Take a manifestation of the element, and turn it into a creature. Something about the element that people fear or find wondrous is particularly fertile ground.<br /> <br /> An earth elemental based on a geode ... wait, no, fuck, that's a Pokemon again, I'm not doing this a second time. Hmm, how about a fear one? The way the wind howls through the trees sometimes and makes your lizard-brain crap itself with dread. Make the beast that makes that sound. Like ... a pack of ephemeral wind-wolves, barely visible in the oncoming twilight, their bodies too long and fluid for real wolves, their fangs as cold as ice. You mistake the first bite for the cold nip of the wind, but then you notice your suddenly numb hand is red with your blood, and see the glowing points of their eyes surrounding you ... shit guys, I've gotta go to bed soon. Look at what you made me do.<br /> <br /> It's winter here, too! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T08:56:13-07:00","id":1221166,"title":"","content":"I remember that one of the previous Exalted books dealt with elementals and mentioned that mixed elemental children or other sources of mixed elements can have a lot of inherent problems. So if you are stuck, take two different elementals, give them a messed up kid and figure out what they can or should do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T09:39:41-07:00","id":1221178,"title":"","content":"Most of my Essence 1-3 ones are just Pokemon by another name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T09:53:15-07:00","id":1221183,"title":"","content":"There are literal truckloads of creatures in legends and mythologies all around the world; I prioritize a good look at them for inspiration (and not just for elementals).<br /> Being also a Shin Megami Tensei fan, I find it easier to give them an elemental or properly otherworldly, bizarre spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T09:54:16-07:00","id":1221185,"title":"","content":"Measure of Hope is right about everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T10:02:39-07:00","id":1221188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals?p=1221185#post1221185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Measure of Hope is right about everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Sigged :P <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T10:53:21-07:00","id":1221209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals?p=1221154#post1221154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An earth elemental based on a geode</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did that, only as a twist on the <i>skogsr\u00e5. </i>The result? A race of hollow, innocent beauties whose insides are studded with gemstones, and who go around inflaming people's greed and lust because they think self-gratification is inherently positive.<br /> <br /> I've also dreamt up a species of animalistic fire elementals with light-based bodies that make them all but invisible in daylight, but blazing beacons in the dark. They're native to the uppermost strata of the sky, and can't effectively fly in the too-thick air of Creation, so the ones heroes might meet and sorcerers might bind are doomed to eternal homesickness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T16:51:32-07:00","id":1221304,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind is, IIRC, that it says somewhere in the fluff that as elementals go up in essence they become more... volatile - they become more one with their elements, which is why the greater elemental dragons are kept locked away, because they're just feral forces of cataclysmic nature.<br /> <br /> So I could imagine a group of very depressed elementals who are miserable that their desire for spiritual enlightenment will result in them basically losing their sanity and becoming feral beasts. Finding a way to cheer them up could make for a fun story","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:50:52-07:00","id":1221762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals?p=1221304#post1221304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind is, IIRC, that it says somewhere in the fluff that as elementals go up in essence they become more... volatile - they become more one with their elements, which is why the greater elemental dragons are kept locked away, because they're just feral forces of cataclysmic nature.<br /> <br /> So I could imagine a group of very depressed elementals who are miserable that their desire for spiritual enlightenment will result in them basically losing their sanity and becoming feral beasts. Finding a way to cheer them up could make for a fun story</div> </div> </div> </div>What might or not be fact, not to mention a particular bit of lore wholly formed in 2e, afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:14:51-07:00","id":1221814,"title":"","content":"Three words: thinly veiled pokem... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals?p=1221178#post1221178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my Essence 1-3 ones are just Pokemon by another name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T18:54:10-07:00","id":1221908,"title":"","content":"Don't know if the OP remember participating on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/859039-elemental-familiars\">this topic</a>, but thought it might be relevant to unearth it from Elsewhere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-24-2018, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T19:55:45-07:00","id":1221922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1220884-need-advice-on-creating-elementals?p=1221188#post1221188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Sigged :P</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Louise was never wrong. She had learned<br /> this to her cost. For most of her life, she<br /> had been certain that she was weak,<br /> stupid, unacademic, and ugly. She was,<br /> of course, correct. Later on, in a foolish<br /> rage from being teased, she announced<br /> that she was smarter than anyone in<br /> the room; and she was, of course, correct.<br /> Understanding in an instant what had<br /> happened, she became strong, dexterous,<br /> academic, and beautiful in a matter<br /> of minutes; and as for those who were<br /> teasing her, she informed them that they<br /> would die in many gruesome ways.<br /> That was not the cost, of course. She had<br /> been certain that she would not regret<br /> their deaths, and she did not. But she<br /> let herself grow arrogant, and one day,<br /> in an argument with a pious man, she<br /> announced that there was no God, no<br /> purpose, no meaning, and no plan to the<br /> universe. And she was, of course, correct.<br /> \u2014from Armor, by Marilith Turner<br /> (From Nobilis the Essentials: Field Guide to The Powers, by Jenna Moran)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> ...it is a terrible burden that you have taken on, friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T08:41:32-07:00","id":1222908,"title":"","content":"Some extra thoughts and a few little useful bits i got while re-reading the 3e core just to shake up ideas.<br /> <br /> - Elementals are <b>not</b> divine representatives or overseers of places, things, or concepts. No portfolio and cosmic role do they fill and any duties or responsibilities are completely self-imposed, by virtue of either choice or coercion, force &amp; manipulation. But beholden to or defined by such things they are not.<br /> <br /> - <b>No </b>spirit-sanctums and temples in (or outside of) Creation await them, except those taken by virtue of either force, guile or luck and even then it is a given/taken abode of a glorified tenant (or squatter).<br /> <br /> - The elemental races are old beyond measure. Before men, before beasts, and some say before even the gods, elementals have stalked Creation, birthed into the world from the interplay of the world\u2019s natural energies. Storm fronts, forest fires, earthquakes, mudslides, deep ocean currents, lightning strikes and blizzards, the heat-haze of the desert and the crushing force of the avalanche are their careless unreponsive deadbeat parents of sorts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside, the idea of elemental races going side by side with primordial races, playing out as either allies, enemies, rivals and/or surrogates to Dragon Kings, Jadeborn, Lintha and a number of the strange beings inhabiting still in the shores of the Dreaming Sea is one particular bit of 3e lore that appeals to me </div> </div> </div>- Being products of the (super)natural cycles of Creation, elementals are beings of the <b>material world</b>, closer to fauna, flora and mortals in perspective and experience than the numinous beings of Yu-shan, Underworld, Malfeas and stranger abodes. Caverns, cities, clouds, deserts, forests, mountains, palaces, plains, ravines, rivers, seas are some of the many other demesnes and places, enchanted or mundane, may they be found on and in some cases decide to call home.<br /> <br /> - Plant, beast, person, monster, hero, devil, god: any or all of those things they may be, alternately or at the same time, depending on their interactions with the physical world around them, whatever crosses their path and leaves a mark upon them, for good or for ill. In that they can be peculiarly strange in many ways and yet curiously similar to the recently Exalted trying to find a place in Creation for themselves and their barely understood powers and urges.<br /> In fact, i wouldn't be surprised if the first exposure of many elementals to the idea of themselves as divine or at least supernatural was through the perspective, first contacts and interaction with mortals, what in itself may bring an interesting twist and angles to their variegated stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Damn, now i'm imagining some people dedicated to seeking out freshly spawned elementals of certain sorts to manipulate into becoming the gods, demigods and heroes of their city-state or nation.<br /> <br /> Or a sorcerer playing a &quot;provider of gods&quot; scam through elemental &amp;/or demon summoning and lots of chicanery. That could be awesome fun too </div> </div> </div>- Sorcerers also bring elementals into form, birthing them through the ritual shaping of sorcerous summoning, a freshly born spirit child whose first act is to either rebel/reject or accept thralldom under its maker. Those particular elementals, originated from the sorcerer's knowledge, ignorance, desires and fancy as much as the elements themselves, may become even more idiosyncratic due to both their origins and their experiences through the period of servitude to the one who molded them. Some may reflect already existing races because it's what the sorcerer needed or wanted, others unique due to combination of desires conscious &amp; unconscious, experimentation and/or a lack of attention/focus in all details or other motives - and if they will stay forever that way or develop through desire or happenstance into the seed of new races, that can be a hook to many tales, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-01-2024, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:25:27-07:00","id":1223192,"title":"","content":"As an aside the &quot;elemental is born out of the Sorcerer's actions/will&quot; angle also brings me to mind images of &quot;matter given form and life&quot;, what in itself opens room for one to play with some elements (duh) of:<br /> <br /> - The faulty or mistreated creation that turns on its creator (Frankenstein, Prague's Golem)<br /> - Those who would make ideal partners for themselves or others (Galatea, Nephele)<br /> - The keeper of an enchanted garden made from the earth that begs for an end of its lonely uniqueness (Adam &amp; Eve)<br /> - FMA's Homunculi i guess.<br /> <br /> And a bunch of other stuff to explore or mine on a number of levels. Though it could be interesting to bring up the possibilities, both in literal making of new elementals ingame and the roleplaying oportunities in the exchange between creature and creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-25-2018, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}